[Music]  i'm jessica chomich morales and i'm a  neuroscientist at the mcgovern institute  at mit  i use a brain imaging technology called  functional magnetic resonance imaging  more commonly known as fmri to see which  regions of the brain become active when  we do certain things  studying the brain is a passion that  arose from being an only child to  immigrant parents i grew up observing  how cultural differences can drive  differences in behavior  my family is from asuncion paraguay this  really oddly shaped country in south  america  i'm producing a neuroscience podcast in  spanish to bring free and valuable  information to the hispanic community i  know from my own experience that there  are not many hispanic people in the  sciences and on top of that most  scientific content is available only in  english  but i'm going to change that  my podcast is called me ultimate  which translates to  my last neuron  i hope to inspire the next generation of  hispanic neuroscientists with this  podcast  [Music]

